;; gate.sexp — rv64gc-lab-v0's evidence manifest for the CPU-SYSTEM gate (P4-SYSTEM.10 slice b).
;; Validate with:
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py gate.sexp schema/gate.sexp
;; Read by scripts/gate_report.py --gate GS, which VERIFIES every declaration here against the
;; tree and holds the list of kinds each axis requires; GS-REPORT.md is its derived output.

(gate (id "CPU-SYSTEM") (profile "rv64gc-lab-v0")
  (statement "The processor gate over the complete declared profile, including its environment contract (ROADMAP.md P4). The open items below were measured by the P4-SYSTEM.10 design brief's census (2026-10-06) and each is owned by a leaf of P4-SYSTEM."))

(evidence (axis G-REGRESSION) (kind directed)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-verify/src/run_rv64gc/tests.rs") (fn "every_guest_matches_its_expectations"))
  (statement "The directed corpus: every tracked guest runs on the engine and its change-observations match the expectations derived spec-side before either engine ran (EVD-05)."))
(evidence (axis G-REGRESSION) (kind external) (record "profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/act4.sexp")
  (statement "The pinned riscv-arch-test suites I, M, Zaamo, Zalrsc, Zca, F and D (318 generated test files, 316,016 signature slots) built with the laboratory's own DUT pieces for this unit and run on this unit's model: every HTIF verdict pass, every signature equal to the Sail-derived one, spike agreeing with Sail as the control pair (P4-SYSTEM.15 slices a–c; the F and D suites with F_SUPPORTED/D_SUPPORTED declared and each file's own TEST_FLEN, 32 or 64). External tests with Sail-derived expectations — one semantics answering twice, never a second independent semantics (EVD-04). Not run: the Misalign suites, whose tests need the framework's trap handler the DUT pieces do not instantiate — and not applicable: they are generated for MISALIGNED_LDST true, and this profile traps misaligned data accesses."))
(evidence (axis G-REGRESSION) (kind validator-mutation)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-verify/src/mutate_rv64gc/tests.rs") (fn "every_designated_mutant_is_detected_by_the_corpus"))
  (statement "The validator-mutation campaign over the complete profile's tables (P4-SYSTEM.15 slice d, EVD-09): 30 designated wrong behaviours across I, M, A, F, D, C, Zicsr and the privileged architecture, each a copy of the generated table with one row changed (a sibling's effect, Nop, the row removed, or one of the two replay controls), run under every one of the 168 tracked guests and compared with the production trace in the corpus rule's own vocabulary. All 30 are detected by at least one guest. Slice d found two the corpus could not tell apart — fle.d exercised only where <= and = agree, c.sub only where - and ^ agree — and pinned them; slice e closed both with one discriminating instruction each (d-compare's fle.d 1.0 <= 2.0, c-alu's c.sub 0 - 3), and the pin is empty: a new gap fails the test. The comparison rule has no suppression knob to misuse (EVD-09's second half is the base profile's mutate suite arm)."))
(evidence (axis G-REGRESSION) (kind generated)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-core/src/fp/tests.rs") (fn "every_spec_side_fixture_holds"))
  (statement "The generated numeric fixtures: the seeded spec-side cases from scripts/gen_fp_vectors.py, each result and flag set derived by the exact-rational authority, held by the model layer (P4-SYSTEM.7)."))
(evidence (axis G-REGRESSION) (kind generated)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-verify/src/m_vectors/tests.rs") (fn "every_generated_vector_holds_through_the_engine"))
  (statement "The generated M vectors: every M instruction over edge and seeded operands, the expected rd from scripts/gen_m_vectors.py's exact-integer reference (RVI-M §11.1, Table 1 by name), run through the engine's decode, guard and operators (P4-SYSTEM.11); the table gated by M-VECTORS."))
;; G-TRACE lists every credited case, its record read from evidence/, with no dossier copy (decision_dossier-copies-retire-at-the-next-window.md; P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3).
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-m-forms-v7")
  (statement "The M case: 33 instructions, 25 finite witnesses (the 13 M forms and the 12 Table 1 cells), a wrong-quotient control observed diverging at step 12. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-m-forms-v7/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-M-5 (REQ-GC-M) is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-xlen-forms-v4")
  (statement "The XLEN case, the first for a state requirement: 25 instructions, 17 finite witnesses, a control expecting the address truncated to 32 bits observed diverging at step 24. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-xlen-forms-v4/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-XLEN-4 (REQ-D-XLEN) is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-csr-set-v3")
  (statement "The CSR-SET case, the first implementation-defined one and on its own reference configuration: 157 steps, 53 finite witnesses, a control expecting a refused write committed observed diverging at step 130. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-csr-set-v3/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-CSR-SET-3 (REQ-D-CSR-SET) is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-zicntr-v3")
  (statement "The ZICNTR case, on the same configuration: 292 steps, 44 finite witnesses, a control expecting a refused read to have committed observed diverging at step 109. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-zicntr-v3/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-ZICNTR-3 (REQ-D-ZICNTR) is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-sstc-v2")
  (statement "The SSTC case, on the same configuration and the first with a delivered interrupt: 315 steps, 39 finite witnesses, a control expecting a signed comparison observed diverging at step 172. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-sstc-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-SSTC-2 (REQ-D-SSTC) is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-alu-imm-v2")
  (statement "The register-immediate forms: 19 steps, 13 finite witnesses, a control expecting an immediate not sign-extended observed diverging at step 12. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-alu-imm-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-ALU-IMM-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-alu-reg-v2")
  (statement "The register-register forms: 18 steps, 10 finite witnesses, a control expecting SLTU read as signed observed diverging at step 11. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-alu-reg-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-ALU-REG-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-lui-auipc-v2")
  (statement "LUI and AUIPC at 64 bits: 10 steps, 9 finite witnesses, a control expecting an offset not sign-extended observed diverging at step 8. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-lui-auipc-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-LUI-AUIPC-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-jalr-lsb-v2")
  (statement "JALR's target and link: 16 steps, 10 finite witnesses, a control expecting a target that keeps its low bit observed diverging at step 3. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-jalr-lsb-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-JALR-LSB-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-no-delay-slots-v2")
  (statement "Control transfers with no delay slot: 21 steps, 11 finite witnesses, a control expecting a slot that ran observed diverging at step 3. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-no-delay-slots-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-NO-DELAY-SLOTS-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-shamt-v2")
  (statement "The twelve shifts' amounts: 21 steps, 15 finite witnesses, a control expecting an amount not masked observed diverging at step 6. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-shamt-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-SHAMT-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-wsuffix-v2")
  (statement "The nine *W forms: 17 steps, 12 finite witnesses, a control expecting a word not sign-extended observed diverging at step 11. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-wsuffix-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-WSUFFIX-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-load-ext-v2")
  (statement "The loads' extension and the stores' widths: 32 steps, 12 finite witnesses, a control expecting LW not sign-extended observed diverging at step 16. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-load-ext-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-LOAD-EXT-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-load-x0-v2")
  (statement "Loads to x0, which still fault: 68 steps, 16 finite witnesses, a control expecting a discarded load to skip its fault observed diverging at step 10. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-load-x0-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-LOAD-X0-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-ecall-ebreak-v2")
  (statement "ECALL and EBREAK from every mode: 116 steps, 25 finite witnesses, a control expecting a cause that does not name its mode observed diverging at step 50. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-ecall-ebreak-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-ECALL-EBREAK-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-csr-access-v2")
  (statement "The six Zicsr forms: 81 steps, 25 finite witnesses, a control expecting a CSR immediate sign-extended observed diverging at step 15. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-csr-access-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-CSR-ACCESS-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-counters-v2")
  (statement "The counter reads and their gates, on the case's own configuration: 84 steps, 8 finite witnesses, a control expecting a refused read to have committed observed diverging at step 23. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-counters-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-COUNTERS-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-fencei-v2")
  (statement "FENCE.I: 18 steps, 4 finite witnesses, a control expecting a stale fetch observed diverging at step 9. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-fencei-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-FENCEI-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-ialign-16-v2")
  (statement "IALIGN of 16: 11 steps, 6 finite witnesses, a control expecting a target rounded to a word observed diverging at step 3. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-ialign-16-v2/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-D-IALIGN-16-2 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-atomics-v1")
  (statement "The A extension's 22 forms at one hart: 246 steps, 64 finite witnesses, a control expecting a word AMO that does not sign-extend observed diverging at step 21. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-atomics-v1/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-ATOMICS-1 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-c-forms-v1")
  (statement "The C selection's 37 forms: 251 steps, 52 finite witnesses, the first case carrying fetch faults, a control expecting C.JALR to link four bytes on observed diverging at step 108. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-c-forms-v1/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-C-1 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-f-forms-v1")
  (statement "The F extension's 30 forms: 338 steps, 90 finite witnesses, a control expecting a static RDN ignored observed diverging at step 127. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-f-forms-v1/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-F-1 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-TRACE) (kind experiment) (experiment "rv64gc-d-forms-v1")
  (statement "The D extension's 32 forms: 350 steps, 93 finite witnesses, a control expecting a static RUP ignored observed diverging at step 131. Its measured record and matched-gpr-v1 verification graph are read from evidence/rv64gc-d-forms-v1/: baseline, byte-identical repeat, every input and observation pinned. Evidence only while CR-GC-D-1 is current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a49-3). Finite evidence, not proof."))
(evidence (axis G-REPLAY) (kind determinism)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-verify/src/run_rv64gc/tests.rs") (fn "every_guest_re_executes_identically_from_cold_reset"))
  (statement "Every guest re-executes identically from cold reset: the run is a function of the definition and the program."))
(evidence (axis G-REPLAY) (kind snapshot)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-verify/src/snapshot_rv64gc/tests.rs") (fn "every_gc_guest_resumes_through_json_with_identical_steps_state_memory_and_fetches"))
  (statement "Every tracked guest is split at three boundaries through JSON snapshots; continued steps, fetch totals, complete final CPU state and memory equal uninterrupted execution, with the same typed laboratory refusals. Reservation/wait effects, TLB slots/FIFO and corrupted/foreign/missing-state refusals have additional controls. This is laboratory snapshot evidence, not board/device or independent ISA validation."))
(evidence (axis G-REPLAY) (kind replay-bundle)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-verify/src/replay_rv64gc/tests.rs") (fn "every_gc_guest_bundle_roundtrips_and_replays_all_recorded_receipts"))
  (statement "Every tracked guest records and replays a self-contained JSON bundle: complete CPU/memory/fault-policy input, explicit no-external-event policy, trace, fetch/model-error receipts and a digest of the complete final checkpoint. Additional controls discriminate trace fields, aggregate/final receipts, foreign identities, invalid states and bounds; four system cases use the real CLI. This demonstrates laboratory reproducibility, not independent ISA correctness or board/device replay."))

(evidence (axis G-REPLAY) (kind reduction)
  (test (file "crates/semulith-verify/src/reduce_rv64gc/tests.rs") (fn "both_controls_reduce_and_replay_the_exact_original_paired_difference"))
  (statement "Both declared full-profile control models reduce with the exact original paired-step difference retained, then replay the deterministic search and both complete reduced-run receipts from self-contained JSON. Mixed 16/32-bit images, a trailing data byte, typed faults, capped search, single-chunk minimality witnesses and damaged record controls have additional tests; both models and capped records use the real CLI. This is bounded laboratory reproducibility, not independent ISA correctness or board/device replay."))

(open (axis G-OBLIGATIONS) (owner "P4-SYSTEM.14")
  (statement "Requirement statuses remain planned except where a current credit record implements one: twenty-three of the 48, and 24 stay planned, routed by decision_obligations-route.md. EVIDENCE_POLICY.md declares the forthcoming requalification policy after the existing implementation; document presence alone proves neither timing nor adequate evidence. P4-SYSTEM.14 still owns structured records, policy/status checks and mirror reconciliation."))
(evidence (axis G-REGRESSION) (kind workload) (record "profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/workload.sexp")
  (statement "The workload suite (P4-SYSTEM.15 slices f and g): four compiled, self-checking, freestanding C workloads under profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/workload/ — integer (M through 64- and 32-bit multiply, divide and remainder), memory, calls and float — built by the pinned toolchain and run three ways, each judged against its Sail-derived signature (4 pass / 0 fail; spike against Sail as the control pair). Compiled programs with Sail-derived expectations: one semantics answering twice, never a second independent semantics (EVD-04). Declared in slice g, once the M case's capture no longer pinned the report generator current (P4-SYSTEM.14 a44-2b)."))
(evidence (axis G-PORTABILITY) (kind aarch64) (record "profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/portability.sexp")
  (statement "P4-SYSTEM.17 slice a: the native leg on this host (cargo test --all) and the fixture digest manifest over the unit's 168 guests; the record is frozen from the run's own logs and digests by scripts/check_portability.sh --profile rv64gc-lab-v0 --record, re-derivable on any host (the legs report that host)."))
(evidence (axis G-PORTABILITY) (kind x86-64) (record "profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/portability.sexp")
  (statement "P4-SYSTEM.17 slice a: the same suites and the same manifest under x86-64 — Rosetta 2 translation on this host, byte-identical to the native digest (the bare-metal leg is the CI matrix's); the record is frozen from the run's own logs and digests by scripts/check_portability.sh --profile rv64gc-lab-v0 --record, re-derivable on any host (the legs report that host)."))
(evidence (axis G-PORTABILITY) (kind miri) (record "profiles/rv64gc-lab-v0/portability.sexp")
  (statement "P4-SYSTEM.17 slice a: the pinned nightly's Miri over semulith-core, natively and on big-endian powerpc64 (the cross-endian leg); the record is frozen from the run's own logs and digests by scripts/check_portability.sh --profile rv64gc-lab-v0 --record, re-derivable on any host (the legs report that host)."))
(open (axis G-RELEASE) (owner "P4-SYSTEM.18")
  (statement "No release decision is recorded for this unit."))
